<DocsLayout
  title="AI assistant"
  subtitle="nikcli is the embedded host. AI SDK v7 is the one-shot path. The package does not store drawings."
  description="CADCAMFUN AI layer: nikcli host, providers, tools, skills, and safety limits."
  toc={toc}
>
  <section id="status" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Status</h2>
    <p>
      WP8 on the task board is <strong>done</strong>. Owner directory: <code>packages/ai</code>
      (<code>@cadcamfun/ai</code>). Spec: <code>specs/08-ai.md</code>. The pinned host is
      <code>@nikcli-ai/sdk-next@1.428.0</code>. Effect stays at <code>4.0.0-rc.112</code> because
      that package requires it. Follow-up contracts in spec 08 (manual compaction wired through
      HTTP, live policy reload, desktop context occupancy) are integration work. The package
      being done does not mean every assistant control in spec 24 is on screen.
    </p>
    <DocCallout type="note" title="Handlers live in the sidecar">
      <p>
        This package registers tools and validates arguments. The sidecar supplies
        <code>ToolHandlers</code> so <code>packages/ai</code> has no SQLite dependency. Mutations
        go through those handlers. Stateless HTTP workflows return suggestions and do not write
        drawings or operations.
      </p>
    </DocCallout>
  </section>

