    <p>
      Sidecar adapters that call this package live in <code>apps/sidecar/src/services/ai.ts</code>
      and the <code>ai-*.ts</code> neighbours (<code>ai-vcs-tools.ts</code>,
      <code>ai-parametric.ts</code>, <code>ai-inspection.ts</code>). Desktop chat is
      <code>apps/desktop/src/features/ai</code>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="host" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Host</h2>
    <p>
      The primary path is <code>NikCli.create(&#123; directory &#125;)</code>. Conversations are
      nikcli sessions (<code>session.create</code>, <code>session.prompt</code>,
      <code>session.abort</code>). The host owns the tool loop and provider routing. The fallback
      is <code>DirectModel</code>: <code>ai</code> v7 with <code>@ai-sdk/anthropic</code>,
      <code>@ai-sdk/openai</code>, <code>@ai-sdk/openai-compatible</code> (MiniMax and any
      compatible base URL), and <code>@ai-sdk/gateway</code>. Use the direct path when the host
      is down or the call is stateless (titles, structured output, a G-code summary).
    </p>
    <DocCode language="ts" title="AiService shape (spec 08 §3)">
{`chat(input): Stream<AiEvent>
analyzeGcode(input): Effect<GcodeReport>
generate(input): Effect<A>
abort(sessionId): Effect<void>
models / providers`}
    </DocCode>
    <p>
      <code>AiEvent</code> is <code>delta</code>, <code>tool_call</code>, <code>tool_result</code>,
      <code>permission_request</code>, <code>done</code>, or <code>error</code>. The same names
      are the SSE contract. <code>ModelSelector</code> is an optional provider, model, and tier
      (<code>fast</code>, <code>balanced</code>, <code>best</code>). One module maps tier to a
      model id. Other files do not hard-code model ids.
    </p>
    <p>
      Safety requirements from spec 08 §1, all tested:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Before create, <code>XDG_DATA_HOME</code>, <code>XDG_CACHE_HOME</code>, <code>XDG_CONFIG_HOME</code>, <code>XDG_STATE_HOME</code>, and <code>NIKCLI_TEST_HOME</code> point under <code>&lt;dataDir&gt;/ai/nikcli/</code>. <code>NIKCLI_DISABLE_PROJECT_CONFIG=1</code>. The host must not read <code>~/.config/nikcli</code>.</li>
      <li>The <code>cadcam</code> agent allow-list is only the tools this package registers, plus the host <code>skill</code> tool. Built-in <code>bash</code>, <code>edit</code>, <code>write</code>, and <code>webfetch</code> stay off the list.</li>
      <li>Permission mode is <code>default</code>. The agent does not auto-approve. Destructive tools require <code>confirm: true</code>.</li>
      <li>Keys pass through <code>Redacted</code>. A sentinel key must not appear in logs.</li>
      <li><code>directory</code> is a scratch folder inside app data, never the user’s home or project directory.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Background work is capped: at most four active workers and sixteen waiting tasks.
      Specialists do not delegate, commit, or open pull requests. The host’s unrestricted
      <code>task</code> tool stays denied. Cancellation holds a slot until the worker stops.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>sdk-next</code> ships JavaScript without <code>.d.ts</code>. Ambient types for the
      surface this package calls live in <code>packages/ai/src/nikcli/sdk-next.d.ts</code>.
      Spec 08 §6 still records the compile-size risk (~20 MB, many dependencies). If
      <code>bun build --compile</code> cannot carry the host, the fallback is a second Bun
      process behind the same <code>AiService</code> interface. That split is a recorded risk,
      not a second architecture you should assume is running.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="credentials" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Credentials</h2>
    <p>
      <code>ProviderId</code> is a string. <code>provider.list()</code> is the catalogue (models.dev
      merged with the isolated <code>nikcli.json</code>). The four providers the app configures
      are <code>anthropic</code>, <code>openai</code>, <code>minimax</code> (default base
      <code>https://api.minimax.io/v1</code>), and <code>gateway</code>. Any other id still needs
      a key before the host will call it. <code>DirectModel</code> only builds clients for those
      four. Another provider on the one-shot path throws and asks for a base URL.
    </p>
    <p>
      Resolution matches the legacy app: use the vendor when its key is set, otherwise the
      gateway. <code>forceGateway</code> sends everything through the gateway.
      <code>PUT</code> and <code>DELETE /ai/credentials</code> check the id against
      <code>GET /ai/providers</code>. A typo is 400 <code>Unknown provider</code>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Keys live in <code>&lt;data dir&gt;/ai/credentials.json</code> (atomic write, mode 0600)
      and in the OS keychain via the Tauri <code>secret_*</code> commands. They are not in
      SQLite and not in <code>LocalKeyValue</code>. The UI reads the keychain at boot and calls
      <code>PUT /ai/credentials</code>. Shutdown clears the host’s copy and leaves the file.
      With <code>NIKCLI_DISABLE_MODELS_FETCH=1</code> the host does not download models.dev.
      <code>makeNikCliRuntime</code> seeds <code>&lt;cache&gt;/models.json</code> once, only when
      the file is missing and <code>catalogue.network</code> is on. The sidecar enables that
      unless <code>CADCAMFUN_AI_OFFLINE=1</code>. The seed does not block boot.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>GET /api/ai/providers</code> is the settings browser. <code>GET /api/ai/models</code>
      is the flat list for the picker, cached for 60 seconds. Optional
      <code>configuredOnly=true</code> filters to providers that have a key.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="tools" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Tools and skills</h2>
    <p>
      Parameter schemas on the host are zod 4. Every handler re-validates with the matching
      Effect schema from <code>@cadcamfun/core</code> before it touches data. A test asserts the
      two schemas accept and reject the same fixtures. Tool results are small JSON. They do not
      include secrets or filesystem paths.
    </p>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Tool</th><th>Effect</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>cad_add_entities</code>, <code>cad_modify_entities</code>, <code>cad_delete_entities</code></td><td>2D entities. Delete requires <code>confirm: true</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>cad_add_elements</code></td><td>Solids, extrude, revolve, sweep, loft, booleans. Invalid input adds nothing and lists every problem.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>cad_describe_drawing</code>, <code>cad_component_list</code></td><td>Read-only counts, bounds, canvas instances.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>cad_component_save</code>, <code>cad_component_insert</code>, <code>cad_component_delete</code></td><td>Library round-trip. Insert mints fresh element ids. Delete confirms.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>cam_create_operation</code>, <code>cam_list_operations</code>, <code>cam_update_operation</code></td><td>WP2 parameter schemas. Update drops stale G-code.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>cam_generate_gcode</code>, <code>cam_suggest_parameters</code>, <code>cam_analyze_gcode</code></td><td>Read-only generation, suggestions, and deterministic checks.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>cam_verify_toolpath</code></td><td><code>cam.verify</code>. Holder, fixtures, and target solids are modelled only when the caller passed them.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>lib_lookup_*</code>, <code>lib_upsert_*</code>, <code>lib_delete</code></td><td>Materials, tools, machine configs, components. Delete confirms. Machine-config delete still follows the library HTTP rules.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>vcs_status</code>, <code>vcs_start_change</code>, <code>vcs_commit</code>, <code>vcs_open_pull_request</code></td><td>Companion flow. An AI actor cannot commit or merge on <code>main</code>. See <a href="/docs/history">History</a>.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>
      Skills in <code>packages/ai/src/skills/index.ts</code> are the playbooks the base agent
      loads: <code>cad-3d-modeling</code>, <code>cam-operation-workflow</code>,
      <code>toolpath-verification</code>, <code>cutting-parameters</code>,
      <code>drilling-and-holes</code>, <code>stock-and-fixtures</code>.
      <code>installSkills</code> writes <code>&lt;config&gt;/skills/&lt;name&gt;/SKILL.md</code>
      whenever host config is written, replacing those folders and leaving others alone. To
      change what the assistant knows, edit that file. To add an ability, add
      <code>tools/&lt;id&gt;.ts</code> and <code>tools/prompts/&lt;id&gt;.txt</code>, list the id
      in <code>tools/registry.ts</code>, and name it from a skill.
    </p>
    <p>
      Tests do not call real providers. A scripted <code>Bun.serve</code> replays SSE for the
      host. <code>DirectModel</code> uses <code>MockLanguageModelV4</code> from <code>ai/test</code>.
      <code>bun run --filter @cadcamfun/ai smoke</code> is the manual real-provider script and is
      excluded from <code>bun test</code>. Host tests share one data directory because
      <code>bun test</code> runs files in a single process. <code>loadSdk</code> resets
      <code>Error.prepareStackTrace</code> around the import so a desktop test cannot break host
      loading.
    </p>
    <p>
      Workspace context and assistant notes use sidecar <code>KvStore</code> over
      <code>LocalKeyValue</code>. Successful stateless workflows use a bounded in-memory LRU
      keyed by normalized input, model selector, and credential revision. Failures are not
      cached. Session chat is not cached.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="boundaries" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Boundaries</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><code>packages/ai</code> must not open the project database. Storage is a handler the sidecar injects.</li>
      <li>The embedded host must not see the user’s nikcli config, shell tools, or home directory.</li>
      <li>API keys must not be logged, put in SQLite, or put in <code>LocalKeyValue</code>.</li>
      <li>G-code optimization and other stateless workflows must not write toolpaths.</li>
      <li>An AI actor must not commit, restore, or merge on <code>main</code>.</li>
      <li>Do not bump Effect in this package alone. The workspace pin moves with <code>sdk-next</code>.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
